      {
        "id": 28904,
        "name": "broccoli",
        "username": "broccoli",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-26T14:37:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>While I’ve done exactly what you’re talking about several times Chris, I’ve also had too many times when I play as many “Draw a Card” cards as I can, and I never find Absolution, Aegis, or Wrathful Retribution, so the end effect is that I have little hp, the only power that does anything is Sacrosanct Martyr (because some effect is reducing all damage by 1, so my base power is useless), and maybe I have a few ongoings out, but I can’t put out Zealous Offense, because I can’t manage the 3 damage, Embolden on myself is a worthless death sentence, and Smite the Transgressor becomes a one-shot that just does 2 damage.</p>\n<p>To be clear, I don’t hate Fanatic.  She commonly pulls off some really neat combos.  My biggest problem with her is that she has several cards that become worthless (including her base power) once all damage is reduced by 1, and in my experience, she often just seems incapable of recovering from a crappy draw.  To be fair, many characters can have bad draws (a friend played a game the other day with Expatriette where he couldn’t draw a gun), but bad draws just seem to happen more often to her, and she seems less able to recover from them.</p>\n<p>All of that said, I have recently come to the conclusion that perhaps I too commonly use a crappy card and/or a slightly ineffectual power when what I should do is skip both and draw 2 cards.  Perhaps if I employ that tactic more readily, I will find myself liking her better.  (And/or maybe her alt’s power will help some <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"> )</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
