      {
        "id": 28910,
        "name": "awp832",
        "username": "awp832",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-27T00:31:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hm…   well I’ll post my contrasting Fanatic strategy.   There are similar elements, but on the whole its quite different.   My way is a bit more conservative and while you won’t be doing as much damage as the way Christopher suggested, you can absorb more and play for the late game.</p>\n<p>Play as many 1 shots that let you draw a card as possible.   So far the same as Christopher.   This I think is relatively critical to any Fanatic strategy.   If you are shut down (you cant deal any meaningful damage because of armor, or doing so would not really be helpful)   you need to draw 2 cards.  Cards will be critical.</p>\n<p>Situationally, Final Dive, Chastise, or Cosecrated Ground will be nice.  If you do not have buffers, Undaunted + Chastise will let you neuteralize a target indefinitely.</p>\n<p>But this is not your “goal”.   Your goal is Divine Focus.   Once that is down clear your hand of Divine Sacrifice, Holy Nova, Embolden, Sacrosanct Martyr…   basically anything that i havent mentioned already aside from Prayer of Desperation.    Use the Prayer on your turn to rinse and repeat as quickly as possible.   You won’t need to do this too often, a few rounds and the villan will be vulnerable to a killing blow with Wrathful Retribution.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:02:51.482Z",
